    h1: "AI for Property Management: How One Property Manager Runs Grok Bots Like Staff",
    dek: "A property manager and broker who runs rentals in several states set up about 20 Grok Bots, from inbox triage to bank reconciliation, and manages them like employees. Here is his hiring framework, the roster, a job-description prompt you can copy, and the guardrails he uses.",
    answerHtml: "<strong>Short answer:</strong> To use AI for property management, treat each bot like a new hire. Start with your pain points and the admin work that keeps people away from owners and tenants. Write a job description for each bot that says exactly what it does, why, and how you'll know it's done. Train it, verify its results, give anything that touches money read-only access, and keep checking as you hand over more.",
